# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event lesson_flame
# en: Putting Fire Out
title [dc5132] = 把火灭掉
# en: Flame is yours now. Professor Thorne gathers the year's new Flame casters in the stone practice room and lights a brazier. "Any fool can start a fire," he says. "You are here to learn to stop one." There is a bucket of water at his feet, and he forbids you to touch it.
text [490b3a] = 火焰咒如今归你了。索恩教授把这一年新学会火焰咒的人召集到石头练习室，点燃一只火盆。“任何蠢货都能生火，”他说，“你们来这儿，是学怎么把火停下。”他脚边有一桶水，他不许你碰。
# en: A stone practice room with scorched walls, a stern grey-bearded professor beside a roaring brazier, a bucket of water at his feet.
scene [dd2300] = 四壁焦黑的石头练习室，一位严厉的灰胡子教授站在熊熊燃烧的火盆旁，脚边一桶水。
# en: Pull the fire back into your hand
opt.left.label [4451c4] = 把火收回手里
# en: You call the flame back like a sleeve pulled over a wrist. It stings, and the brazier flares and sinks. "Again," says Thorne. He says it eleven times.
opt.left.say.1 [c20bd6] = 你把火焰召回，就像把袖子拉回手腕。手被灼得生疼，火盆窜起又落下。“再来，”索恩说。他说了十一遍。
# en: Ask what the bucket is for
opt.right.label [f6e8aa] = 问那桶水是干什么的
# en: "For the student who doesn't ask," says Thorne, and empties it over the brazier of the boy beside you. Then he explains, for an hour, how every great fire he has known began.
opt.right.say.1 [933d3a] = “给不提问的学生用的，”索恩说着，把整桶水浇在你旁边那个男生的火盆上。然后他花了一个钟头，讲他见过的每一场大火是怎么烧起来的。

@event lesson_tide
# en: Waist-Deep at Dawn
title [82cbf9] = 黎明时齐腰深
# en: Professor Marisol teaches Tide where it lives: waist-deep in the lake at dawn. "Cold water," she says happily, "is good for everyone." She recites a poem about waves and stops before the last line, frowning. The lake waits for you.
text [7c2f23] = 玛丽索尔教授在潮涌咒住的地方教它：黎明时，湖里齐腰深的水中。“冷水，”她高兴地说，“对谁都有好处。”她背了一首关于海浪的诗，在最后一行前停住，皱起眉头。湖水在等你。
# en: A misty lake at dawn, a professor standing waist-deep in the water with arms raised, students hesitating on the pebbled shore.
scene [93a9d4] = 黎明时雾气蒙蒙的湖，一位教授站在齐腰深的水里高举双臂，学生们在卵石岸边犹豫不前。
# en: Wade in and call a wave
opt.left.label [103d24] = 蹚进水里唤一道浪
# en: The water is so cold it feels like an opinion. Your wave rises knee-high and slaps Marisol full in the chest, and she whoops. "The last line!" she shouts. "It was about this!"
opt.left.say.1 [10fb6d] = 水冷得像一种观点。你唤起的浪只有膝盖高，正正拍在玛丽索尔胸口，她欢呼起来。“最后一行！”她喊，“写的就是这个！”
# en: Call it from the shore
opt.right.label [a49270] = 在岸上施咒
# en: You work the spell from the dry pebbles and raise a neat little swell. Marisol looks at your dry boots with real sorrow, as if at a poem with no ending.
opt.right.say.1 [0ca97b] = 你站在干燥的卵石上施咒，掀起一道整整齐齐的小浪。玛丽索尔看着你干爽的靴子，真心实意地难过，像在看一首没有结尾的诗。

@event lesson_foresight
# en: The Bottom of the Cup
title [d6ff5b] = 杯底
# en: The astromancy lecturer, who wears three scarves in every season, sits the class at the observatory with cups of tea and no instructions. Foresight, it turns out, begins at the bottom of the cup: what you think you see, and what you want to.
text [4e84c1] = 那位一年四季围三条围巾的星象讲师，让全班坐在观星台里，每人一杯茶，什么也不讲。原来，预见始于杯底：你以为自己看见了什么，和你想看见什么。
# en: An observatory room with tea cups on every desk, a lecturer in three scarves peering into a student's cup with a magnifying glass.
scene [abb57c] = 观星台的房间里每张桌上都放着茶杯，一位围着三条围巾的讲师拿放大镜窥看学生的杯子。
# en: Read your own cup
opt.left.label [130c28] = 读你自己的杯子
# en: The leaves say a hard week is coming. It does, from Tuesday. The lecturer says that's the trouble with reading your own: you start making it true.
opt.left.say.1 [fdc255] = 茶叶说，艰难的一周就要来了。从周二开始，果然来了。讲师说，读自己的杯子麻烦就在这儿：你会开始让它成真。
# en: Read your neighbour's
opt.right.label [661301] = 读邻座的杯子
# en: You tell your neighbour a letter is on its way. A letter arrives at supper. Now half the dormitory wants their leaves read, and you have to learn to say "unclear" kindly.
opt.right.say.1 [15b70b] = 你告诉邻座，有封信在路上。晚饭时信就到了。现在半个宿舍都想让你读茶叶，你只好学会温和地说“看不清”。

@event lesson_starlight
# en: A Jar on the Roof
title [346e45] = 屋顶上的罐子
# en: Starlight is practised after midnight on the observatory roof, where your Starcalling tutor hands you a glass jar and tells you to hold it up "until something falls in". The stars are very far away. The roof is very cold.
text [a2c014] = 星光咒是午夜后在观星台屋顶上练的。你的唤星术导师递给你一只玻璃罐，让你举着，“直到有东西掉进去”。星星非常远。屋顶非常冷。
# en: A flat observatory roof at night, a student holding up a glass jar toward a sky crowded with stars, breath steaming.
scene [64cb32] = 夜里平坦的观星台屋顶，一个学生朝满天繁星举起玻璃罐，呼出的气冒着白雾。
# en: Hold the jar until it fills
opt.left.label [72681d] = 举着罐子，直到装满
# en: At three in the morning a thread of light settles in the jar like milk in tea. You carry it down the stairs in both hands. You can't feel your fingers until breakfast.
opt.left.say.1 [12b784] = 凌晨三点，一缕光沉进罐子里，像牛奶落进茶里。你双手捧着它下楼。直到早饭时，你的手指都没有知觉。
# en: Lie back and watch the sky
opt.right.label [3f4130] = 躺下看星空
# en: You lie on the roof and name the constellations with whoever is beside you. Your jar stays empty. The lecturer, passing, says that's the first lesson too, and the one most people skip.
opt.right.say.1 [ad51ae] = 你躺在屋顶上，和身边的人一起数星座。你的罐子一直空着。讲师路过时说，这也是第一课，而且是大多数人跳过的那一课。

@event lesson_mend
# en: Teacups First
title [606e4e] = 先修茶杯
# en: Sister Amaranth teaches Mend with teacups. She drops one on the infirmary floor without looking. "Mend it." When it's whole she drops another. "Bones are harder," she says, rolling bandages. "Cups first."
text [bd4c39] = 阿玛兰斯修女用茶杯教愈合咒。她看都不看就把一只茶杯摔在医务室地上。“修好它。”修好了，她又摔一只。“骨头更难，”她一边卷绷带一边说，“先修杯子。”
# en: An infirmary storeroom, a stern healer dropping a teacup to the stone floor while a student kneels over the pieces with a wand.
scene [32aa56] = 医务室的储藏间，一位严厉的医者把茶杯摔在石地上，一个学生拿着魔杖跪在碎片旁。
# en: Mend cup after cup
opt.left.label [0314eb] = 一只接一只地修
# en: By the twentieth cup you can hear the crack close before you see it. Amaranth says "Keep doing that," and drops a teapot.
opt.left.say.1 [0628fd] = 修到第二十只，你还没看见裂缝合上，就先听见了。阿玛兰斯说“继续这样做”，然后摔了一只茶壶。
# en: Ask her about the bones
opt.right.label [4f800c] = 问她骨头的事
# en: She tells you, still rolling bandages, about the worst break she ever set. It was a student's; that student is a professor now. You go a little pale, and listen to every word.
opt.right.say.1 [37dcc5] = 她一边卷绷带，一边给你讲她接过的最糟的一次骨折。那是个学生的；那个学生现在当了教授。你脸色有点发白，但一字不落地听完了。

@event lesson_purify
# en: Make It Stronger
title [fcd954] = 让它更浓
# en: Sister Amaranth has heard that Pell taught you to Distill. She sets a cauldron of something green in front of you that she will not name. "Pell teaches it fast," she says. "I teach it so you're still standing afterwards. Make it stronger." Then she goes back to her own work.
text [4c9d1e] = 阿玛兰斯修女听说佩尔教会了你萃取。她把一锅不肯说名字的绿色东西放在你面前。“佩尔教得快，”她说，“我教的是让你萃完还站得住。让它更浓。”说完她回去忙自己的了。
# en: An alchemy lab bench with a cauldron of thick green liquid, a healer standing over a student who holds a wand above it.
scene [77f705] = 炼金实验室的工作台上一锅浓稠的绿色液体，一位医者站在举着魔杖的学生身边。
# en: Distill it drop by drop
opt.left.label [a3f178] = 一滴一滴地萃取
# en: Drop by drop, the green comes down to one dark spoonful, and each drop costs you a little. You sit down halfway, as she said you would. Amaranth tastes the result, nods and puts it on the high shelf.
opt.left.say.1 [9cf12d] = 一滴又一滴，那锅绿色浓缩成深色的一勺，每一滴都从你身上拿走一点。萃到一半你坐了下来，正如她说的那样。阿玛兰斯尝了尝成果，点点头，把它放上了高架。
# en: Ask what it was
opt.right.label [210c34] = 问那是什么
# en: "Last term's soup," she says. You decide not to believe her, then decide you do. She shows you where to stop before it takes too much from you, and you distill half a cup, badly.
opt.right.say.1 [b138c3] = “上学期的汤，”她说。你决定不信，然后又决定信。她教你在它从你身上拿走太多之前停手，你萃了半杯，萃得很糟。

@event lesson_glamour
# en: Pick a Card
title [760613] = 抽一张牌
# en: Professor Vey's glamour lesson is a card game. Each student glamours a plain card to look like the queen of stars, and Vey picks out the true queen from the pile. Nobody, she says, has ever made her pick wrong. "Fool me, and you may skip the essay."
text [952f53] = 维伊教授的魅影课是一场纸牌游戏。每个学生把一张普通的牌伪装成星辰皇后，维伊从一堆牌里挑出真正的皇后。她说，从来没人让她挑错过。“骗过我，就可以免交论文。”
# en: A velvet-curtained classroom, a professor in a violet coat fanning out a hand of playing cards toward a row of students.
scene [dce887] = 挂着天鹅绒帘子的教室，一位穿紫罗兰色外套的教授把一手扑克牌扇形展开，朝向一排学生。
# en: Glamour your card
opt.left.label [0c0fb9] = 给你的牌施魅影
# en: Vey picks your card, turns it over and finds a plain two. She laughs out loud, a real laugh, and the class goes silent. "Well," she says. "Well, well. No essay for you." By supper the whole tower knows, and Vey has started calling you "my card sharp".
opt.left.say.1 [3f0a00] = 维伊挑中你的牌，翻过来，是一张普通的二。她放声大笑，真心的笑，全班鸦雀无声。“好，”她说，“好，好啊。你不用交论文了。”到晚饭时全塔都知道了，维伊开始叫你“我的老千”。
# en: Vey passes over your card without a glance. "The queen of stars," she says kindly, "does not blush." But you saw how she chose: by the hands, not the cards.
opt.left.say.2 [8f34d2] = 维伊看都没看就略过了你的牌。“星辰皇后，”她和气地说，“是不会脸红的。”可你看清了她是怎么挑的：看手，不看牌。
# en: Watch how she catches them
opt.right.label [be78bf] = 看她怎么识破
# en: You watch her eyes instead of the cards. She never looks at the faces, only at the hands holding them. You write that down, and she sees you write it, and smiles.
opt.right.say.1 [1511f9] = 你不看牌，看她的眼睛。她从不看牌面，只看拿牌的手。你把这点记下来，她看见你在记，笑了。

@event lesson_mirror
# en: Gently
title [99b2bc] = 温柔些
# en: Professor Vey teaches Mirror in an empty classroom with the curtains drawn, which is not like her. "A mirror charm shows people themselves," she says. "Do it gently. Most people have not asked to see." She stands to one side of every glass in the room.
text [0cc1d8] = 维伊教授在一间拉上窗帘的空教室里教镜像咒，这不像她。“镜像咒让人看见自己，”她说，“要温柔些。大多数人没要求看。”教室里每一面镜子，她都站在旁边避开。
# en: A dim classroom with the curtains drawn, a hand mirror on every desk, a professor standing well to one side of the glass.
scene [927d45] = 拉上窗帘的昏暗教室，每张桌上一面手镜，一位教授远远地站在镜子侧面。
# en: Practise on yourself first
opt.left.label [8a2034] = 先在自己身上练
# en: The charm shows you yourself a moment too honestly. You practise until you can look at it without flinching. Mostly.
opt.left.say.1 [f32110] = 咒语让你看见的自己，诚实得过了一点。你一直练到能看着它不躲闪。差不多吧。
# en: Ask why she avoids the glass
opt.right.label [42aa1b] = 问她为什么躲开镜子
# en: "Vanity," says Vey, with a magnificent smile that answers nothing at all. But she lets you stay after the others leave, and shows you how to soften the charm's edges.
opt.right.say.1 [ffe355] = “虚荣，”维伊说，露出一个华丽的笑容，什么也没回答。不过别人走后她让你留下，教你怎么把咒语的锋芒磨软一些。

@event lesson_haste
# en: Race the Hippogriff
title [8af651] = 和鹰头马身有翼兽赛跑
# en: Professor Brask teaches Haste on the flight field, with a stopwatch and a hippogriff that is faster than the spell. "Beat her," she says to you. To the hippogriff she explains, at length and politely, that she is not to bite you if you win.
text [165778] = 布拉斯克教授在飞行场教疾速咒，拿着一块秒表，还有一头比咒语还快的鹰头马身有翼兽。“赢过她，”她对你说。然后她又对那头兽客客气气、详详细细地解释：你要是赢了，不许咬你。
# en: A windy flight field marked with flags, a grey-haired professor holding a stopwatch, a student sprinting beside a hippogriff.
scene [57e5ef] = 插着旗子的飞行场上风很大，一位灰发教授拿着秒表，一个学生在鹰头马身有翼兽旁边飞奔。
# en: Race the hippogriff
opt.left.label [691071] = 和它赛跑
# en: You cross the flag a beak's length ahead. The hippogriff looks at Brask; Brask looks at the stopwatch, then at you. "Hm," she says. From her, it's a medal.
opt.left.say.1 [d51c8e] = 你领先一个喙的长度冲过旗子。那头兽看着布拉斯克；布拉斯克看着秒表，又看看你。“嗯，”她说。从她嘴里出来，这就是一枚奖章。
# en: The hippogriff wins by a length and takes your hat as her prize. Brask tells a story about a student who lost to a goose. It ends with a bite. "Moral: faster."
opt.left.say.2 [4beef4] = 那头兽领先一个身位赢了，还把你的帽子叼走当奖品。布拉斯克讲了个学生输给一只鹅的故事。结尾是被咬了一口。“寓意：快点。”
# en: Time the others first
opt.right.label [f5b3cc] = 先给别人计时
# en: You hold the stopwatch and watch the fast ones. They aren't running harder; they start the spell a step before they need it. Brask sees you notice, and hands you the next race.
opt.right.say.1 [38d0ad] = 你拿着秒表看跑得快的人。他们并没有跑得更用力；他们在需要之前一步就起咒了。布拉斯克看出你注意到了，把下一场比赛交给了你。
# en: Afterwards you ask her how to start the spell a step early yourself. She shows you, and remembers that you asked.
opt.right.say.2 [dcbb36] = 之后你问她，自己该怎样提前一步起咒。她教了你，并且记住了你开口问过。

@event lesson_beast_speech
# en: The Mule Has Views
title [ec4453] = 骡子有看法
# en: Beast-speech, says Professor Brask, is mostly listening. She sits you in a stall beside an old mule who has, she says, "views". You are to hear them. The mule looks at you as if you're the one being taught.
text [460ee4] = 布拉斯克教授说，兽语大部分是倾听。她让你坐在一个畜栏里，旁边是一头老骡子，她说它“有看法”。你得听出来。骡子看着你，好像你才是来受教的那个。
# en: A warm stall with straw on the floor, a student sitting cross-legged opposite a grey old mule who stares back without blinking.
scene [13f579] = 铺着稻草的温暖畜栏，一个学生盘腿坐着，对面一头灰色老骡子一眨不眨地回瞪。
# en: Sit with him all afternoon
opt.left.label [32ae78] = 陪它坐一下午
# en: In the fourth hour the mule's thoughts come through: mostly apples, and one long grievance about a farrier. Brask says "Good," to the mule, not to you.
opt.left.say.1 [b8cda1] = 第四个钟头，骡子的想法传了过来：大多是苹果，还有一大段对某个钉马掌的人的抱怨。布拉斯克说“好”，是对骡子说的，不是对你。
# en: Try the spell straight away
opt.right.label [59b22b] = 直接施咒
# en: You cast before you've listened and get one word back, very clearly: "Rude." Brask laughs once, loudly. It's the laugh of the term, and everyone in the stables heard it.
opt.right.say.1 [9b7054] = 你还没听就施了咒，清清楚楚地收到一个词：“无礼。”布拉斯克大笑了一声。这是本学期的那一声笑，整个马厩都听见了。

@event lesson_ward
# en: Chalk
title [e38b98] = 粉笔
# en: At the top of the lecture tower, where the lamps burn dim on purpose, the umbral lecturer drills first-years in their Ward by throwing chalk. Hard, and without warning. "A ward that only works when you're ready," says the lecturer, "is a decoration."
text [0d49cc] = 讲堂塔顶上，灯故意点得很暗，暗影讲师用扔粉笔的方法训练新生的护界。扔得很狠，毫无预兆。“只在你准备好时才管用的护界，”讲师说，“是装饰品。”
# en: A dim room at the top of a tower, low lamps, a lecturer mid-throw with a piece of chalk while students hold up shimmering wards.
scene [066bb6] = 塔顶昏暗的房间，灯光低垂，一位讲师正扔出一截粉笔，学生们举着微微发光的护界。
# en: Hold the ward all hour
opt.left.label [2d1be2] = 撑住护界一整节课
# en: The first chalk hits your forehead. The fifth bounces off the ward with a sound like a bell. By the end of the hour your ward is up before you know you've raised it.
opt.left.say.1 [c53b86] = 第一截粉笔砸中你的额头。第五截从护界上弹开，响得像一声钟。到下课时，你的护界在你意识到之前就已经立起来了。
# en: Watch the lecturer's wrist
opt.right.label [965178] = 盯着讲师的手腕
# en: You let the ward drop and watch how the throws begin. Three pieces of chalk find your forehead while you do. But you see it now: the shoulder moves first.
opt.right.say.1 [2c86ff] = 你放下护界，观察每一次投掷是怎么开始的。这期间有三截粉笔砸中了你的额头。但你看出来了：先动的是肩膀。

@event lesson_shadowstep
# en: Where the Voice Was
title [9b35f0] = 声音在的地方
# en: Shadowstep is taught in the dark. The umbral lecturer puts out the last dim lamp and calls your name from somewhere else in the room. You have to arrive where the voice was before it moves. Somewhere, a chair is waiting for your shins.
text [05e14f] = 影步是在黑暗里教的。暗影讲师熄灭最后一盏暗灯，从房间别处叫你的名字。你得在声音移开之前，到达它刚才所在的地方。某处有一把椅子，正等着你的小腿。
# en: A pitch-dark tower room with one dim lamp guttering out, the outline of a student stepping between deep shadows.
scene [877abd] = 漆黑的塔中房间，一盏暗灯即将熄灭，一个学生的轮廓正踏入深深的阴影之间。
# en: Step into the dark
opt.left.label [2680ac] = 踏进黑暗
# en: You step, and the dark folds, and you're across the room with a bruise from the chair. The voice is right beside you. "Better," it says, and moves away again.
opt.left.say.1 [25eb2c] = 你迈出一步，黑暗折叠起来，你已到了房间另一头，腿上被椅子撞出一块青。声音就在你身边。“好一点了，”它说，又移开了。
# en: Wait for your eyes to adjust
opt.right.label [565cb0] = 等眼睛适应
# en: You stand still until the dark has edges. The lecturer, somewhere, says that's cheating, and that cheating is half of umbral magic. You step only once, but you step exactly.
opt.right.say.1 [98d714] = 你一动不动，直到黑暗有了边缘。讲师在某处说这是作弊，而作弊是暗影魔法的一半。你只迈了一步，但这一步分毫不差。

@event lesson_animate
# en: The Chair That Follows
title [d19868] = 跟着走的椅子
# en: The Artifice homework is to animate something and live with it for a day. You pick a chair, which follows you to every lecture. The teapot is the other option. It has opinions about being carried.
text [d289ff] = 奇械术的作业是活化一样东西，和它一起过一天。你挑了一把椅子，它跟着你去上每一节课。另一个选项是茶壶，它对被人提着走颇有意见。
# en: A workshop corridor, a wooden chair trotting after a student like a dog, a teapot waddling behind it.
scene [ffbfad] = 工坊走廊里，一把木椅像小狗一样小跑着跟在一个学生身后，后面还摇摇摆摆跟着一只茶壶。
# en: Live with the chair
opt.left.label [76d3db] = 和椅子过一天
# en: The chair follows you everywhere and offers itself whenever you stop, including on the stairs, at speed. By evening you have bruised shins and a very loyal chair.
opt.left.say.1 [8427ee] = 椅子走到哪儿跟到哪儿，你一停下它就凑上来让你坐，包括在楼梯上、全速的时候。到傍晚，你的小腿青一块紫一块，换来一把非常忠心的椅子。
# en: Animate the teapot instead
opt.right.label [4d6ebe] = 改为活化茶壶
# en: The teapot waddles after you all day, pouring when you sit. It takes more out of you than the chair would, but your friends have never been so well looked after.
opt.right.say.1 [fd76ab] = 茶壶摇摇摆摆地跟了你一整天，你一坐下它就倒茶。它比椅子更耗你的力气，但你的朋友们从没被照顾得这么周到过。

@event lesson_seal
# en: Only for the Addressee
title [372311] = 只给收信人
# en: Today's Hollow Studies exercise: seal a letter so that only the person it's addressed to can open it. The headmistress will try to open it first. "If I can," she says mildly, "you haven't."
text [f31824] = 今天空洞研究的练习：封好一封信，让只有收信人才能打开。院长会先试着打开。“要是我打得开，”她温和地说，“你就没封住。”
# en: A windowless room, a student pressing their thumb to a folded letter while a headmistress watches with her hands folded.
scene [7faf91] = 一间没有窗户的房间，一个学生把拇指按在一封折好的信上，一位院长双手交叠地看着。
# en: Seal it against her
opt.left.label [8b087d] = 封住，防着她
# en: She tries the letter for a long minute with one finger, then hands it back unopened. "Better than I was at your age," she says, which doesn't sound like a compliment. You feel hollowed out till supper.
opt.left.say.1 [42dc8e] = 她用一根手指试了足足一分钟，然后把信原封不动地还给你。“比我在你这个年纪时强，”她说，听上去不像夸奖。直到晚饭你都觉得被掏空了。
# en: Ask how she'd break it
opt.right.label [902617] = 问她会怎么破解
# en: She shows you, kindly and very quickly, how she'd break yours. You leave the room knowing a great deal more about seals and rather less sure of your own.
opt.right.say.1 [6b2748] = 她和气地、飞快地给你演示了她会怎么破你的封。离开时你对封缄懂得多了，对自己的封却没那么有把握了。

@event lesson_wildfire
# en: Longer Each Night
title [8c3b43] = 一夜长过一夜
# en: Lyra wants you in the duel hall after hours. "You let it go too early," she says, and lights her own. "Hold it. Longer each night. It will bite you; let it."
text [4e22f7] = 莱拉要你下课后来决斗厅。“你松手松得太早了，”她说着点起自己的火，“握住它。一夜比一夜久。它会咬你；让它咬。”
# en: An empty duel hall at night, two students each holding a growing fire, one watching the other's with narrowed eyes.
scene [1f034f] = 夜里空荡荡的决斗厅，两个学生各自握着一团不断长大的火，其中一人眯着眼盯着另一人的火。
# en: Hold it until it bites
opt.left.label [1580f1] = 握到它咬人
# en: You hold it until the heat is in your teeth and then a breath longer. When you let it go it runs to the rafters. Lyra looks at your blistered palm and says nothing, which is approval.
opt.left.say.1 [37eafe] = 你一直握到热气钻进牙缝，然后再多握一口气。一松手，它直奔房梁。莱拉看着你起泡的掌心，什么也没说，这就是认可。
# en: Ask her how she stands it
opt.right.label [be5a97] = 问她怎么受得了
# en: She doesn't answer at first. Then she shows you her palms, scarred and old, and tells you about the first time, and her mother. You don't practise much. It's still the right night.
opt.right.say.1 [d54a01] = 她起初没回答。然后她给你看了她的掌心，伤痕累累，是旧伤，讲了第一次的事，还有她的母亲。你没怎么练。这一晚依然是对的。

@event lesson_heartwood
# en: A Tree by the Window
title [2d71f6] = 窗边的一棵树
# en: Tobias wants you to grow a heartwood every evening for a week, "so your hands remember". Today he suggests the courtyard under your dormitory window, where nothing has grown in years.
text [ad5103] = 托比亚斯要你连续一周每晚都种一棵心木，“好让你的手记住”。今天他提议种在你宿舍窗下的庭院里，那里好几年没长过东西了。
# en: A dormitory courtyard at dusk, a young tree that wasn't there that morning, two students sitting under it looking pleased with themselves.
scene [c8ec59] = 黄昏的宿舍庭院，一棵早上还不存在的小树，两个学生坐在树下，一脸得意。
# en: Grow it properly, roots and all
opt.left.label [c091b7] = 好好种，连根带枝
# en: It takes everything you've got and a blister. By dusk there's a young tree under your window, and your back aches like a harvest. Tobias says it's the best one he's seen, and apologises for saying so.
opt.left.say.1 [8496a0] = 这用尽了你所有的力气，还磨出一个水泡。到黄昏，你窗下立着一棵小树，你的背酸得像收了一季麦子。托比亚斯说这是他见过最好的一棵，又为这么说道了歉。
# en: Sit under his instead
opt.right.label [709e57] = 改坐在他的树下
# en: You let him grow it and sit under it with him, talking about nothing. Your hands don't remember much. The rest of you does.
opt.right.say.1 [a1dc24] = 你让他来种，和他一起坐在树下闲聊。你的手没记住多少。你其余的部分记住了。

@event lesson_omen
# en: The Spoon Will Fall
title [67cae0] = 勺子会掉
# en: At breakfast Seraphine says, without looking up, "Practise on small things. Spoons. Doors. The weather. Never people, not yet." Then she looks at you, quite clearly, for once.
text [55b703] = 早饭时，瑟拉芬头也不抬地说：“在小事上练。勺子。门。天气。别用在人身上，还不行。”然后她看着你，难得地清清楚楚。
# en: A refectory table at breakfast, a pale student pointing at a spoon balanced on the edge of a bowl, a second student staring at it.
scene [0de841] = 早饭时膳堂的长桌，一个苍白的学生指着一把搭在碗沿上的勺子，另一个学生盯着它看。
# en: Foretell small things all day
opt.left.label [5b12d1] = 一整天预言小事
# en: The spoon falls. The door sticks. It rains at four. By evening it unnerves you how well it works, and you catch yourself foretelling the soup.
opt.left.say.1 [8a1997] = 勺子掉了。门卡住了。四点下雨了。到傍晚，它灵验得让你发毛，你发现自己在预言汤。
# en: Ask what "not yet" means
opt.right.label [daf7eb] = 问“还不行”是什么意思
# en: "Later," she says, then, "I mean that exactly." She doesn't explain. She does pass you the salt before you've asked for it.
opt.right.say.1 [9395cc] = “以后，”她说，接着说，“我就是字面意思。”她没解释。不过你还没开口，她就把盐递了过来。

@event lesson_sleight
# en: Pockets and Decks
title [d97053] = 口袋与牌堆
# en: Corvin is teaching you to keep your hand in. "Decks are practice," he says, shuffling. "Pockets are performance." Bram is asleep in an armchair nearby, his whistle on a ribbon round his neck.
text [e4450d] = 科尔文在教你保持手感。“牌堆是练习，”他洗着牌说，“口袋是表演。”附近一张扶手椅上，布拉姆睡着了，他的哨子用缎带挂在脖子上。
# en: A dim corner of a common room, a grinning student fanning a deck of cards while another student palms a coin under the table.
scene [f184cd] = 公共休息室昏暗的角落，一个咧嘴笑的学生展开一副牌，另一个学生在桌下藏起一枚硬币。
# en: Practise on the deck
opt.left.label [c7e5c3] = 拿牌堆练
# en: Two hours of coins and cards until your fingers cramp. It's dull, and by the end the coin vanishes so cleanly even Corvin blinks. "Saint," he says, "with very quick hands."
opt.left.say.1 [d449a1] = 两个钟头的硬币和纸牌，练到手指抽筋。很枯燥，但到最后硬币消失得干净利落，连科尔文都眨了眨眼。“圣人，”他说，“手很快的那种。”
# en: Lift Bram's whistle and return it
opt.right.label [66b534] = 摸走布拉姆的哨子再还回去
# en: The whistle comes off its ribbon without a sound and goes back on it the same way. Bram snores through all of it. Corvin is delighted and slightly worried about you.
opt.right.say.1 [e0a626] = 哨子无声无息地离开缎带，又同样无声无息地回去。布拉姆从头打鼾到尾。科尔文乐坏了，又有点替你担心。

@event lesson_contraption
# en: The Breakfast Engine
title [42c819] = 早餐引擎
# en: Mir slides a breakfast tray across to you. "Practice! Make it do breakfast. Toast, butter, tea. It's the hardest machine there is, probably." Half the refectory has already turned to watch.
text [d21132] = 米尔把一只早餐托盘推到你面前。“练习！让它做早餐。吐司、黄油、茶。这是世上最难的机器，大概吧。”半个膳堂已经转过头来看了。
# en: A breakfast table where a clattering machine made of a toast rack, a spoon and a teapot is buttering toast at alarming speed.
scene [be285b] = 早餐桌上，一台由吐司架、勺子和茶壶拼成的机器正咔嗒作响，以惊人的速度往吐司上抹黄油。
# en: Build the breakfast engine
opt.left.label [9d4c5d] = 造早餐引擎
# en: Your engine butters four slices, pours one cup and singes your eyebrow before it falls apart in a shower of crumbs. The refectory applauds. Mir writes something down, beaming.
opt.left.say.1 [cf3c7b] = 你的引擎抹了四片黄油，倒了一杯茶，燎了你一根眉毛，然后在一阵面包屑雨中散了架。膳堂鼓起掌来。米尔笑容满面地记下了什么。
# en: Build it with Mir, slowly
opt.right.label [500d56] = 和米尔慢慢造
# en: You build it together, Mir explaining every joint. It makes one perfect slice of toast and then retires. Mir says it's the best machine of the year, probably.
opt.right.say.1 [9461a7] = 你们一起造，米尔讲解每一个接头。它做出了一片完美的吐司，然后退休了。米尔说这是今年最好的机器，大概吧。

@event lesson_hoarfrost
# en: Putting Out Fires
title [3a4863] = 灭火
# en: "It's for putting fires out," Kael says again, and nods across the duel hall to where Lyra is practising, very loudly, with a very large flame. He waits to see whether you'll take the hint.
text [a79905] = “这是用来灭火的，”凯尔又说了一遍，朝决斗厅另一头点点头，莱拉正在那儿非常响亮地练着一团非常大的火。他等着看你会不会领会。
# en: A duel hall where one student's flame is frosting over and going out, its caster glaring, a quiet student standing nearby.
scene [812686] = 一座决斗厅，一个学生的火焰正在结霜熄灭，施法者怒目而视，一个安静的学生站在旁边。
# en: Put out Lyra's flame
opt.left.label [d5a941] = 冻熄莱拉的火
# en: Your frost meets her flame and they cancel with a hiss and a cloud of steam. Lyra's face, when it clears, is magnificent. Kael makes a sound you think is a laugh.
opt.left.say.1 [6a4da5] = 你的霜迎上她的火，两者嘶的一声在一团蒸汽中抵消了。蒸汽散去时莱拉的表情精彩极了。凯尔发出一个你觉得是笑的声音。
# en: Practise on the braziers instead
opt.right.label [61fdba] = 改拿火盆练
# en: You frost the braziers one by one. It's useful, and dull, and Kael stays with you for all of it without saying anything. You suspect that was the point.
opt.right.say.1 [e38212] = 你一个个给火盆结霜。有用，也枯燥，凯尔一直陪着你，一句话没说。你怀疑这才是重点。

@event lesson_candour
# en: Questions People Want to Answer
title [a15e8c] = 别人想回答的问题
# en: Nessa hands you a notebook in the refectory. "Three people, three true answers, by the end of lunch," she says. "Ask the question they want to answer. Use the spell only when you have to."
text [d16f34] = 内莎在膳堂递给你一个笔记本。“三个人，三个真话，午饭结束前，”她说，“问他们想回答的问题。只有不得已时才用咒语。”
# en: A busy refectory, a bossy editor pointing out students at random tables to another student holding a notebook.
scene [487f75] = 热闹的膳堂，一位颐指气使的编辑随手指着各桌的学生，另一个学生拿着笔记本。
# en: Use the spell on all three
opt.left.label [38e831] = 三个人都用咒语
# en: Three truths by the pudding course, and one of them is about you, and not kind. Nessa reads your notes and says, "Now you know why I don't use it much."
opt.left.say.1 [5231a1] = 布丁上桌时你已经拿到三句真话，其中一句是关于你的，而且不太客气。内莎读完你的笔记说：“现在你知道我为什么不常用了。”
# en: Ask good questions instead
opt.right.label [30a254] = 只凭问得好
# en: You only manage two truths without the spell, but they're good ones, and nobody minded telling you. Nessa says that's the better trick, and that she won't print either.
opt.right.say.1 [e030fc] = 不用咒语你只拿到两句真话，但都很好，而且没人介意告诉你。内莎说这是更好的本事，还说两句都不会登。

@event lesson_brace
# en: Planted
title [5ea443] = 站稳
# en: The eyepatched dummy is empty now, but it still throws a hex or two out of habit. The Circle uses it to practise bracing. Today the seniors are taking bets on how long you'll stand.
text [f44646] = 那个戴眼罩的假人现在空了，但出于习惯还会扔出一两道恶咒。决斗社用它练坚守。今天高年级生们在打赌你能站多久。
# en: A duel hall's practice corner, an eyepatched dummy firing weak hexes at a student who stands planted and unmoving.
scene [c00534] = 决斗厅的练习角落，一个戴眼罩的假人朝一个学生扔出软弱的恶咒，学生站得稳稳的，一动不动。
# en: Stand until it gives up
opt.left.label [727463] = 站到它放弃
# en: You stand there for an hour while the dummy throws everything it has left. The seniors pay out to whoever bet longest. Your shins are a mess and you are unmovable.
opt.left.say.1 [835744] = 你在那儿站了一个小时，假人把剩下的一切都扔了过来。高年级生们赔钱给押时间最长的人。你的小腿一塌糊涂，人却纹丝不动。
# en: Coach the first-years instead
opt.right.label [6d90f5] = 改去指导新生
# en: You stand behind a row of first-years and fix their feet, one by one, while they get hexed. They're grateful. You're bored. The dummy throws one at you on the way out, out of spite.
opt.right.say.1 [082447] = 你站在一排新生身后，一个个纠正他们的站姿，他们挨着恶咒。他们很感激。你很无聊。你出门时假人朝你扔了一道，纯属泄愤。

@event lesson_quickquill
# en: Lecture Notes
title [c0b410] = 课堂笔记
# en: Your quill wants to take your lecture notes for you. It writes everything down, word for word, faster than the lecturer can talk. It also writes what it thinks of the lecturer, in the margins.
text [bbcb65] = 你的羽毛笔想替你记课堂笔记。它一字不落，比讲师说得还快。它还在页边写下了它对讲师的看法。
# en: A lecture hall, a quill writing busily by itself in a notebook while its owner sits back with folded arms, the lecturer squinting at them.
scene [a03909] = 一间讲堂，一支羽毛笔在笔记本上自己忙着写，主人抱着胳膊往后靠，讲师眯眼看着他们。
# en: Let it take the notes
opt.left.label [468c14] = 让它记笔记
# en: You have perfect notes, every word, and a margin full of the quill's views on the lecturer's waistcoat. You spend the evening inking them out before anyone sees.
opt.left.say.1 [52f4b1] = 你有了完美的笔记，一字不差，还有满满一页边羽毛笔对讲师马甲的高见。你花了一晚上用墨涂掉它们，免得被人看见。
# en: Make it take only what you say
opt.right.label [db7273] = 让它只记你说的
# en: It sulks, and then takes down exactly what you tell it, no more. It's work keeping it honest. You come out with half the notes and the full trust of your quill.
opt.right.say.1 [847ea4] = 它闹了会儿脾气，然后一字不多地记下你让它记的。管住它不说谎可费劲。你只得到一半的笔记，却得到了羽毛笔全部的信任。

@event lesson_bramble
# en: A Hedge on Demand
title [680c51] = 随叫随到的树篱
# en: Old Maud has heard about your hedge. "There's a gap in my fence the rabbits use, dearie," she says. "Grow me one there. Thorns on the outside, mind." The rabbits are watching from the cabbages.
text [729710] = 老莫德听说了你的树篱。“我篱笆上有个缺口，兔子老从那儿钻，亲爱的，”她说，“给我种一道。刺朝外，记着。”兔子们在卷心菜地里看着。
# en: Old Maud's cottage garden, a groundskeeper pointing at a gap in her fence while a student coaxes a thorny hedge up out of the ground to fill it.
scene [dea0bc] = 老莫德小屋的花园，一位园丁指着篱笆上的缺口，一个学生正哄着一道带刺的树篱从地里长出来填补它。
# en: Grow it thorns and all
opt.left.label [3d5051] = 连刺一起种
# en: The hedge comes up thick and thorny, and takes a strip off your knuckles on the way. Maud inspects it and says it'll do. The rabbits look betrayed.
opt.left.say.1 [67c5a8] = 树篱长得又密又多刺，冒出来时还刮掉了你指节上一层皮。莫德检查了一番，说行。兔子们一脸被背叛。
# en: Grow it gently, for the cabbages
opt.right.label [529a7c] = 种得温和些，为了卷心菜
# en: You grow it soft and plant a row of cabbages beyond it for the rabbits. Maud laughs until she has to sit down. "You'll understand that in two weeks," she says.
opt.right.say.1 [2c37a8] = 你把它种得很软，又在外面给兔子们种了一排卷心菜。莫德笑得不得不坐下。“过两个星期你就明白了，”她说。

@event lesson_index
# en: The Right Page
title [8bae11] = 对的那一页
# en: Every book you touch falls open at the page you need, now. The trouble is the library knows it, and books are leaving their shelves to come and find you. Footnote is sitting on the biggest.
text [7d6f48] = 现在你碰到的每本书都会翻到你需要的那一页。麻烦在于图书馆知道了，书纷纷离开书架来找你。脚注坐在最大的那本上。
# en: A library table piled with heavy books, every one falling open at a different marked page as a student touches it, a cat watching from the top of the pile.
scene [40e94c] = 一张堆满厚书的图书馆长桌，学生碰到哪本，哪本就翻开到不同的标记页，一只猫在书堆顶上看着。
# en: Read every page they offer
opt.left.label [019527] = 读完它们送上的每一页
# en: You read every page that offers itself until the lamps go out. You learn a great deal, most of it useful, and none of it what you came in for.
opt.left.say.1 [1c13c9] = 你读每一页送上门来的书，直到灯熄。你学到很多，大部分有用，没有一样是你来找的。
# en: Find one thing for your exams
opt.right.label [f27744] = 只找一样考试要的
# en: You ask for one thing, firmly. Twelve books bring it. You take your page and leave the others, who sulk on the table until a clerk shelves them.
opt.right.say.1 [31f3f8] = 你坚定地只要一样东西。十二本书都送来了。你拿了你那一页就走，其余的在桌上生闷气，直到一位职员把它们放回去。

@event lesson_rapport
# en: A Room That Was Turning
title [660228] = 一屋子正要翻脸的人
# en: Two tables in the refectory are on the edge of a food fight, and every head is turning. It's the Newt all over again, with worse gravy.
text [9b4121] = 膳堂里两张桌子眼看要打一场食物大战，所有人都转过头来。这简直是蝾螈酒馆重演，只是肉汁更难吃。
# en: A refectory at supper where two tables are on the edge of an argument, a student stepping between them with a raised mug and a grin.
scene [078221] = 晚饭时的膳堂，两张桌子眼看要吵起来，一个学生举着杯子笑着走到中间。
# en: Step in and turn it
opt.left.label [fbcbbf] = 上前扭转局面
# en: One joke about the gravy, at exactly the right moment, and both tables laugh instead of throwing it. The prefects look relieved and slightly suspicious. Your heart doesn't slow down until bed.
opt.left.say.1 [5bef0c] = 在恰好的时刻说一句关于肉汁的笑话，两桌人笑了，没有扔。级长们松了口气，又有点起疑。你的心跳直到睡前才慢下来。
# en: Let it happen
opt.right.label [e54ca5] = 随它去
# en: You let it go, and the food fight is magnificent. You watch from under the table, laughing. Nobody remembers it was nearly stopped.
opt.right.say.1 [6bc4ce] = 你随它去，这场食物大战壮观极了。你躲在桌子底下笑着看。没人记得它差点被拦下。

@event lesson_tailwind
# en: Never Stop
title [fd9083] = 永不停下
# en: The fisherman's rule for the wind is "never stop". You take the long way round the lake on your free afternoon to practise it, and the wind gets behind you as soon as you're off the jetty.
text [c7f206] = 渔夫关于风的规矩是“永不停下”。你在空闲的下午绕湖远飞去练，刚离开码头，风就绕到了你身后。
# en: A student on a broom skimming low over a lake at tremendous speed, a wake of spray behind them and a fisherman waving from a boat.
scene [5023b4] = 一个学生骑扫帚贴着湖面极速掠过，身后溅起一道水花，一个渔夫在船上挥手。
# en: Never stop
opt.left.label [dd27a3] = 永不停下
# en: You go round the lake three times without stopping, faster each lap, until your hands are numb on the handle. The fisherman waves every lap now.
opt.left.say.1 [dedab4] = 你绕湖三圈，一刻不停，一圈比一圈快，直到握扫帚柄的手冻麻了。现在渔夫每一圈都挥手。
# en: Land and talk to him
opt.right.label [2bd58c] = 落下来和他聊聊
# en: You land by his boat and tell him about the storm run. He listens, nods, and says, "Never stop," again, and hands you a fish to take home.
opt.right.say.1 [dc479a] = 你落在他的船边，给他讲了风暴那趟。他听着，点点头，又说了一遍“永不停下”，递给你一条鱼带回家。

@event lesson_lodestar
# en: The Lighthouse Light
title [20cc48] = 灯塔之光
# en: The light gathers round your shoulders in Grimsby's shop without your meaning it to, and the old man puts down his pen. "Lodestar," he says softly. "A lighthouse keeper's spell. She used it to walk the lamp-stair in storms." He doesn't say who she was. You think you know.
text [375d35] = 在格林斯比的店里，光不由自主地聚到了你肩头，老人放下了笔。“引星，”他轻声说。“灯塔看守人的咒语。她在暴风雨里靠它走灯塔的楼梯。”他没说她是谁。你觉得你知道。
# en: An old bookseller in a dark shop watching a soft guiding light gather around a student's shoulders, his spectacles reflecting it.
scene [7fe392] = 昏暗的书店里，一位老书商看着一团柔和的引路之光聚在学生的肩头，眼镜上映着那光。
# en: Ask him to watch you cast it
opt.left.label [ee990d] = 请他看你施咒
# en: You let the light build, breath by breath, until it stands round you like a lantern. Grimsby nods along to your breathing, as if to a tune he knows. "Slower," he says. "She was always slower."
opt.left.say.1 [90c2df] = 你让光一口气一口气地聚起来，直到它像一盏灯笼一样围着你。格林斯比随着你的呼吸点头，像在跟一支他熟悉的曲子。“慢一点，”他说。“她总是更慢一些。”
# en: Ask about the lighthouse
opt.right.label [d77ac4] = 问问灯塔的事
# en: He tells you about the lamp, the stair, the keeper who wanted to see a long way, and the books she bought from him for forty years. The light round your shoulders stays lit the whole time, listening.
opt.right.say.1 [824783] = 他跟你讲那盏灯，那道楼梯，那个想看得很远的看守人，还有她四十年来从他这儿买的书。你肩头的光一直亮着，一直在听。

@event lesson_moonwell
# en: Sitting Still
title [41cd49] = 静坐
# en: Old Maud finds you on her garden bench at dusk, trying to make Moonwell go faster. She sits down beside you. "That's your trouble," she says. "It's a sitting-still spell, dearie. You can't hurry a basin."
text [b0f0a7] = 黄昏时，老莫德发现你坐在她花园的长凳上，想让月泉来得快一点。她在你身边坐下。“这就是你的毛病，”她说。“这是个静坐的咒语，亲爱的。石盆是催不来的。”
# en: An old woman and a student sitting on a garden bench under the moon, eyes closed, a faint silver light pooling in the student's cupped hands.
scene [8c5c9d] = 月光下，一位老妇人和一个学生坐在花园长凳上，闭着眼，学生捧着的双手里积着一点淡淡的银光。
# en: Sit still with her
opt.left.label [54e6c0] = 陪她静坐
# en: You sit until the moon is up and your feet are cold. Somewhere in the second hour, the light starts pooling, and you stop trying, and it fills. Maud is asleep. You don't wake her.
opt.left.say.1 [085c4a] = 你一直坐到月亮升起，脚都冷了。第二个小时里的某一刻，光开始积聚，你不再用力，它就满了。莫德睡着了。你没叫醒她。
# en: Ask how she knows the spell
opt.right.label [be9857] = 问她怎么会这个咒语
# en: "Learned it in the wood," says Maud, "same as you, sixty years back. Everybody who goes deep enough learns it eventually. The ones who come back, anyway." She pats your knee as if that were reassuring.
opt.right.say.1 [0e8952] = “在林子里学的，”莫德说，“跟你一样，六十年前。走得够深的人迟早都会学会。至少是那些回来了的人。”她拍拍你的膝盖，好像这话很让人安心。

@event lesson_reflect
# en: Hall of Mirrors
title [785523] = 镜廊
# en: Professor Vey hears you've learned Reflect and appears in the mirror corridor with a bag of very small, very harmless hexes. "Show me," Vey says, and throws one at your head.
text [64d864] = 维伊教授听说你学会了反照，就带着一袋非常小、非常无害的恶咒出现在镜廊里。“露一手，”维伊说，然后朝你脑袋扔了一个。
# en: A theatrical professor in a corridor of mirrors throwing a small spell at a student, who sends it bouncing back down the corridor.
scene [08a5e9] = 镜子走廊里，一位很有舞台感的教授朝一个学生扔出一个小咒语，学生把它沿着走廊弹了回去。
# en: Send it back
opt.left.label [aed0d3] = 弹回去
# en: You catch the hex and return it. Vey ducks, delighted, and throws three. You return two. The third gives you rabbit ears for an hour, which Vey says is the lesson.
opt.left.say.1 [7f4a36] = 你接住恶咒，弹了回去。维伊高兴地一躲，扔了三个。你弹回去两个。第三个让你长了一小时的兔耳朵，维伊说这就是这一课。
# en: Send it somewhere else
opt.right.label [92bf64] = 弹到别处去
# en: You catch the hex and bounce it off a mirror into a suit of armour, which sneezes. Vey laughs so hard the mirrors ring. "Oh, you're going to be trouble."
opt.right.say.1 [50f320] = 你接住恶咒，让它在一面镜子上弹了一下，飞进一副盔甲里，盔甲打了个喷嚏。维伊笑得镜子都在响。“噢，你以后会是个大麻烦。”

@event lesson_rime
# en: Cold Enough
title [207a71] = 够冷了
# en: Kael sees the frost at your collar and goes still. "Rime," he says. "Where did you... no. Don't tell me." He looks at {season == "winter": the snow|the courtyard, and frost runs out from his boots across the flagstones}. "In the North we learn it as children. You don't feel the cold less. You just stop letting it decide things."
text [2f332e] = 凯尔看见你衣领上的霜，一下子僵住了。“雾凇，”他说。“你从哪儿……不。别告诉我。”他看着{season == "winter": 雪|庭院，霜从他的靴底蔓延出去，铺满了石板}。“在北方，我们小时候就学这个。你并不会觉得没那么冷。你只是不再让冷来替你做决定。”
# en: A pale Northern student and another student standing in a frost-whitened courtyard, frost spreading from their collars, breath steaming.
scene [895b91] = 结满白霜的庭院里，一个苍白的北方学生和另一个学生站着，霜从他们的衣领蔓延开，呼吸冒着白气。
# en: Let him show you
opt.left.label [a35ef6] = 让他教你
# en: He makes you stand in {season == "winter": the snow|the cold he's laid on the flagstones} until it hurts, and then until it doesn't, and then a while longer. When you go in, he's almost smiling. "Now it's yours," he says.
opt.left.say.1 [e6b6d8] = 他让你站在{season == "winter": 雪里|他铺在石板上的寒气里}，一直站到疼，再站到不疼，然后再多站一会儿。你们进屋时，他几乎在笑。“现在它是你的了，”他说。
# en: Ask what else they learn as children
opt.right.label [4921a8] = 问他们小时候还学什么
# en: "Not to want things," he says, and then looks as if he wishes he hadn't. He leaves before you can ask anything else. The frost at your collar feels colder.
opt.right.say.1 [d5279c] = “不去想要东西，”他说，然后一副后悔说出口的样子。你还没来得及再问，他就走了。衣领上的霜感觉更冷了。

@event lesson_siphon
# en: The Fern on the Sill
title [82797f] = 窗台上的蕨
# en: You're tired, and there are lectures at eight, and there's a fern on your windowsill, green and full of life it isn't using. Siphon is right there in your hands. Nobody would ever know but the fern.
text [73569c] = 你很累，明早八点还有课，窗台上有一盆蕨，绿油油的，满是它用不上的生命。虹吸就在你手里。除了那盆蕨，没人会知道。
# en: A student at a dormitory window at night with a hand hovering over a potted fern, the fern's leaves beginning to curl.
scene [2f67ab] = 夜里，一个学生站在宿舍窗前，手悬在一盆蕨上方，蕨叶开始卷曲。
# en: Just a little
opt.left.label [ee6350] = 就一点点
# en: The fern greys from the tips inward. You feel wonderful. You throw the fern out in the morning, before anyone sees it.
opt.left.say.1 [d7ac4f] = 蕨从叶尖开始往里变灰。你感觉好极了。早上，你赶在别人看见之前把那盆蕨扔了。
# en: Go to bed tired
opt.right.label [6f4bc5] = 累着去睡觉
# en: You go to bed tired, and wake tired, and the fern is green. You water it, which feels like an apology to something.
opt.right.say.1 [f67a10] = 你累着上了床，累着醒来，那盆蕨是绿的。你给它浇了水，感觉像是在向什么东西道歉。

@event lesson_compel
# en: "Again"
title [357cd7] = “再来”
# en: A first-year drops a stack of books in the corridor, and laughs at themselves, and you could say the word. "Again." They'd drop them again, and again, and never know why. It would be funny. That's the worst part: it would be funny.
text [18a208] = 一个一年级生在走廊里把一摞书掉在了地上，还自嘲地笑了，而你可以说出那个词。“再来。”他们会把书再掉一次，一次又一次，永远不知道为什么。那会很好笑。这才是最糟的：那会很好笑。
# en: A student in a castle corridor watching another student drop a stack of books, a word forming on their lips.
scene [84d873] = 城堡走廊里，一个学生看着另一个学生掉了一摞书，嘴唇正在组成一个词。
# en: Say it, once
opt.left.label [d536d0] = 说一次
# en: They drop the books again, and stare at their hands. You walk on quickly. It wasn't funny.
opt.left.say.1 [b16160] = 他们又把书掉了，盯着自己的手。你快步走开了。一点也不好笑。
# en: Help pick them up
opt.right.label [aa8624] = 帮忙捡起来
# en: You pick up half the books and the first-year thanks you twice. The word stays in your mouth, unused, like a stone you could throw.
opt.right.say.1 [814c2f] = 你捡起了一半的书，那个一年级生谢了你两次。那个词留在你嘴里，没用出去，像一块你本可以扔出去的石头。

@event lesson_torment
# en: The Shape of It
title [0e26e7] = 它的形状
# en: Sparring in the duelling hall, you feel Torment rise in your hand like a reflex. You stop it. Professor Thorne, across the hall, saw something: he's looking at you the way he looks at a fire in the wrong place.
text [a99348] = 在决斗厅里对练时，你感到折磨像一种本能一样在你手里升起。你止住了它。决斗厅那头的索恩教授看见了什么：他看你的眼神，像在看一团烧错了地方的火。
# en: A stern grey-bearded professor in a duelling hall looking hard at a student whose wand hand has frozen mid-cast.
scene [dfc983] = 决斗厅里，一位严厉的灰胡子教授紧盯着一个学生，学生的持杖手僵在施咒的半途。
# en: Tell him
opt.left.label [bcfe3c] = 告诉他
# en: You tell him. He listens without a word, then says, "Then you know what it costs. Most people learn that afterwards." He gives you extra drills for a month, which you suspect is kindness.
opt.left.say.1 [48273a] = 你告诉了他。他一言不发地听着，然后说：“那你就知道它的代价了。大多数人是事后才知道的。”他给你加了一个月的训练，你怀疑这是一种好意。
# en: As you leave he adds that he lost to the storm because he didn't stop in time. You knew already. You've never heard him say it like that.
opt.left.say.2 [79fd1d] = 你要走时他补了一句：他输给那场风暴，是因为没有及时停手。你早就知道了。但你从没听他这样说过。
# en: Say it was nothing
opt.right.label [4f60bd] = 说没什么
# en: "Nothing, sir." He doesn't believe you. He doesn't say so. He watches you spar for the rest of the term.
opt.right.say.1 [596353] = “没什么，先生。”他不信。他没说出来。那一学期剩下的时间里，他一直看着你对练。

@event lesson_extraction
# en: Someone Else's Spark
title [3e3d67] = 别人的火花
# en: In a study group, the student beside you is casting a little light to read by, and you can feel their magic like warmth from a stove. Extraction would take it. They'd feel tired, that's all. You've got so much to do.
text [36f616] = 在学习小组里，你旁边的学生点着一点光照着读书，你能感觉到他们的魔力，像炉子的热气。汲取能把它拿走。他们只会觉得累，仅此而已。而你还有那么多事要做。
# en: A study group around a library table at night, one student's quill glowing with magic, another student staring at it hungrily.
scene [8b35f2] = 夜里图书馆桌旁的学习小组，一个学生的羽毛笔闪着魔光，另一个学生饥渴地盯着它。
# en: Take a little
opt.left.label [5e0faf] = 拿一点点
# en: Their light gutters. They yawn, rub their eyes, and go to bed early. You study until dawn on someone else's magic, and remember none of it.
opt.left.say.1 [2b4d40] = 他们的光暗了下去。他们打了个哈欠，揉揉眼睛，早早去睡了。你靠别人的魔力学到了天亮，什么都没记住。
# en: Lend them yours instead
opt.right.label [c52238] = 把你的借给他们
# en: You light the table yourself so they can rest their hand. They grin at you. The hunger goes quiet, for now.
opt.right.say.1 [fdc096] = 你自己把桌子照亮，好让他们歇歇手。他们冲你咧嘴一笑。那份饥渴安静了下来，暂时。

@event lesson_eclipse
# en: The Burn
title [ef83b1] = 烫伤
# en: You burn your hand on a cauldron in the lab, badly. And Eclipse wakes up: the pain could be power, it says, all of it, held and ready. You'd still feel the burn. You'd just have something to show for it.
text [c2aa09] = 你在实验室里被坩埚烫伤了手，烫得很厉害。然后蚀醒了：它说，这疼痛可以变成力量，全部，攒着，随时可用。你还是会感觉到烫伤。你只是会有点东西可以拿出来。
# en: A student in an alchemy lab clutching a burnt hand, a faint dark glow gathering around the injury.
scene [b92a5d] = 炼金实验室里，一个学生捂着被烫伤的手，伤处周围聚起一圈淡淡的暗光。
# en: Hold the pain
opt.left.label [dcf061] = 攒住这份疼
# en: You let the burn become power and carry it all day like a coal in your pocket. It's very strong. It still hurts. Both of those stay true.
opt.left.say.1 [e20e0d] = 你让烫伤变成力量，一整天都揣着它，像兜里揣着一块炭。它非常强。它也还是疼。两件事都一直是真的。
# en: Go to the infirmary
opt.right.label [f09b9c] = 去医务室
# en: Sister Amaranth dresses it and tells you off for daydreaming. The power you didn't take aches a little, like a tooth.
opt.right.say.1 [5193c9] = 阿玛兰斯修女给你包扎好，数落你走神。那份你没拿的力量隐隐作痛，像一颗牙。

@event lesson_heartprice
# en: Paying in Yourself
title [716107] = 用自己付账
# en: It's late, {mana < 15: your Mana is spent|your Mana is low and tomorrow has a practical}, and the essay isn't done. Heartprice says you don't need Mana. You have yourself. You could pay in that, for as long as you can stand it.
text [dea4cb] = 夜深了，{mana < 15: 你的魔力用光了|你的魔力所剩无几，明天还有实践课}，论文还没写完。心价说你不需要魔力。你有你自己。你可以用它来付，付到你撑不住为止。
# en: An exhausted student at a desk late at night, a faint red glow in their chest feeding a spell, candles burnt down.
scene [530e5f] = 深夜里，一个筋疲力尽的学生坐在桌前，胸口一点淡淡的红光在为一个咒语供能，蜡烛已经燃尽。
# en: Pay in yourself
opt.left.label [202fcd] = 用自己付
# en: You finish the essay on your own strength. In the morning your hands shake and the essay is very good. You don't feel proud of it.
opt.left.say.1 [56beb6] = 你靠自己的力气写完了论文。早上你的手在抖，论文写得非常好。你并不为它感到骄傲。
# en: Leave it for tomorrow
opt.right.label [69476d] = 留到明天
# en: You go to bed with the essay unfinished. It's worse than it would have been. You're better than you would have been.
opt.right.say.1 [6e9f49] = 你带着没写完的论文上了床。它会比本来的样子差一些。你会比本来的样子好一些。
